        narrative: "Meiji Shrine's forest in the morning, then Omotesando and Harajuku on foot, then Shinjuku as the lights come on. These three sit close enough together that you can walk the whole day with one train ride at the end, which is unusual in Tokyo and worth exploiting.\n\nThis is also the right day for something specific rather than general. A neighbourhood food walk down a genuine local shopping street tells you more about how Tokyo eats than a night in an expensive restaurant will, and it solves dinner. If you would rather cover ground than eat, an e-bike through the backstreets does in three hours what would take a full day on foot.\n\nPack tonight, not tomorrow morning. Tomorrow you move.",
