        narrative: "Take a morning train down to Odawara and pick up the Shinkansen west. Two hours later you are in Kyoto, and if you forwarded your suitcase it is already at the hotel. Drop your day bag and start walking.\n\nNishiki Market is the obvious first stop and best treated as lunch rather than a sight: pickles, tamagoyaki, skewers and the basement food halls of the nearby department stores, which are quietly better than the market itself. From there the Gion lanes and the Shirakawa canal fill an afternoon on foot.\n\nSave Fushimi Inari for after dark. The shrine is open 24 hours and unstaffed at night, the tunnel of vermilion gates is lit, and the crowds that make it unbearable by day are gone entirely. It is a 5-minute train ride from Kyoto Station on the JR Nara line. This is the single best thing a short Kyoto stop can do, and almost nobody plans it.",
